We start by computing the probabilities that a single phase of \OI usages leads to a certain fitness improvement. From the way we constructed the Markov chain, the length $Z_k$ of each phase is independent from the solution $x_{T_s^{(k)}}$ it starts with (and hence its fitness $y_{T_s^{(k)}}$), and follows a geometric law.
