%    Let $\mathcal{S} \subset \R_+$ be a finite state space of non-negative reals with $0 \in \mathcal{S}$ and $(x_t)_{t \geq 0}$ a sequence of random variables over $\mathcal{S}$. Let $T = \inf\{ t \geq 0 \mid x_t = 0\}$ then, if there exists a $\delta > 0$ such that for all $t \geq 0$ and all $s \in \mathcal{S} \setminus \{0\}$  we have
%        \[ \esp[x_t - x_{t + 1} \mid x_t = s] \geq \delta, \]
%    then
