A WFA is \emph{deterministic} if it has a single initial state, and from every state there exists at most one finite-weight transition on each letter. It is \emph{determinizable} if it has an equivalent deterministic WFA (i.e., they describe the same function). 
It is well-known that not every WFA is determinizable~\cite{chatterjee2010quantitative}. In this paper, we show that determining whether a WFA is determinizable is decidable.


