\section{Experiment}

\subsection{Experimental Setup}

To comprehensively evaluate MLLMs’ understanding of traditional Chinese culture, we select various MLLMs, including both open-source and closed-source models. For open-source MLLMs, we choose models with different parameter sizes. Specifically, the selected open-source models are: LLaVA-v1.6-7B/34B~\citep{liu2024visual}, DeepSeek-VL-7B~\citep{lu2024deepseekvlrealworldvisionlanguageunderstanding}, Qwen2-VL-7B/72B~\citep{wang2024qwen2vlenhancingvisionlanguagemodels}, CogVLM2-19B~\citep{wang2023cogvlm}, GLM-4V-9B~\citep{glm2024chatglm}, InternVL2.5-8B/78B~\citep{chen2024far}. We use A800 GPUs to deploy and evaluate them. For closed-source MLLMs, we choose GPT-4o\cite{openai2024gpt4o}, Claude-3.7 Sonnet~\citep{claude3.7sonnet} and Gemini-2.0 Flash\cite{gemini2025}. We evaluate them by calling the corresponding official APIs. The prompts are formatted as a multiple-choice setup. Following MMMU~\citep{yue2024mmmu}, we use accuracy as the evaluation metric and prepare a rule-based answer extraction method. More detailed experimental setups can be found in Appendix~\ref{appendix:experi_detail}.


