\section{Possible extensions of existing fairness measures for one multi-valued sensitive attribute}
\label{appx:extension}

Here we list the possible extensions of existing fairness measures for one multi-valued sensitive attribute, that is, $a_1\!\in\! \mathcal{A}\!=\!\mathcal{A}_1\!=\! \{1,2,...,n_{a_1}\}$, $n_a\!=\!1$, $n_{a_1}\!\geqslant\! 2$, and $n_{a_1}\!\in\!\mathbb{Z}_+$. 
Note that $a_1\!=\!1$ is still used to denote a member that belongs to the privileged group, and in this case, only one privileged group exists. 
All four extensions apply to this case, while only the third and fourth extensions apply to scenarios when more than one privileged groups exist. 



\subsection{Group fairness measures following the independence criterion}

\begin{proposition}[Extensions of demographic parity, Definition~\ref{def:grp1,dp}]
\begin{subequations}
\topequation\small
\begin{align}
