\subsection{Bridging 2D Sketches and 3D Geometries with the CAD Agent}



In this section, we introduce the \textit{CAD Agent}\footnote{To avoid confusion, we differentiate it from the Meshing Agent, which focuses exclusively on generating computational meshes for CFD simulations.}, which bridges conceptual sketches and detailed 3D car designs. Given a 2D hand-drawn sketch, the CAD Agent searches the DrivAerNet++ database in real-time to retrieve the most similar existing 3D design. Beyond retrieval, it can perform generative tasks, synthesizing novel 3D designs and interpolating between two input models to explore intermediate shapes, all conditioned on industry-standard automotive geometries. This facilitates rapid exploration and generation of feasible, production-oriented concepts.




