Given the latent codes of two or more car models, a weighted average of these codes produces a new latent representation that blends features of the input designs. When decoded by the DeepSDF network, the resulting shapes are visually plausible and maintain realism, showcasing the latent space's ability to capture meaningful geometric relationships and support novel design generation.


