A configuration of the machine $M$ at any moment of computation consists of a state $q\in Q$
and the contents of the tape in the form $x \in (\Gamma \cup K)_*$.
An input $(x_1, \dots, x_n) \in \Sigma^*$ is initialized as
$(\ldots , b\textbf{.}\, x_1, \ldots ,x_n, b,\ldots) \in (\Gamma \cup K)_*$.

The transitions of $M$ are defined in the following manner.
Let $q$ be the current state and let $a$ be the current tape symbol.
