The element $z$ determines the symbol to be written on the tape under the head of the machine
so that, if $z \in \Gamma \cup K$,
the symbol $z$ is written, and if $z = \operatorname{id}$, the symbol $a$ is not changed,
and if both $z = (\star, r)$ and $a \in K$ are true, then the value of the operation
$a \star v$ is written on the tape, where $v$ is the current value of the register $r$.
In other cases $M$ halts.

