\begin{definition}[First-order logic with (in)equality]
    The syntax for the first-order logic (of a  vocabulary $\tau$) with formula (in)equality 
    %over a positive and commutative (ordered) semiring $K$ 
    for a set $O\subseteq\{{=,}{\neq,}{\leq,}{\not\leq}\}$, denoted by $\FO(O)$, is defined as follows:
    %\[
     %     \phi\ddfn \alpha \mid \alpha \circ \alpha \mid (\phi \wedge \phi) \mid (\phi \lor \phi) \mid \exists x\phi \mid \forall x\phi,
     %\]
