    Then for any $F \subseteq \arbF$ we define the syntax of $\FO(O, F)$ $\tau$-formulae  by extending the Backus--Naur form for $\FO(O)$ formulae by the rule
    $
        \alpha \Coloneqq P_f(\ol{x}) %\mid \neg P(\ol{x}),
    $,
    where $P_f \in \sigma_F$ and $\ol{x}$ is a tuple of variables such that $\lvert \ol{x} \rvert = \ar(P)$.
\end{definition}

