\end{split}
\end{align}
Observe that for a linear thresholding missingness pattern, the set $\{\mb{y}: \obs(\mb{y})=A, \mb{y}_A=\mb{x}\}$ is convex for any set $A$ and any $\mb{x} \in \R^{|A|}$. Using the fact (Corollary 2.1 of \cite{KP77}) that the variance of a Gaussian is non-increasing when restricted to a convex set:

\[
