\subsubsection{Trust value calculation}

In this model, we proposed two types of edge servers: a global edge server and a local edge server. The global edge server has the responsibility to manage the local edge servers. The user service requests are collected by the local edge server. Then, we calculate the trust value for the edge server as follows:

\begin{equation}
     \tau (LE) = In_\tau \pm (1- In_\tau) X \vartheta
\end{equation}

where, $In_\tau$ and $\vartheta$ denote the initial trust value and degree of change of trust value of the edge servers, respectively. Based on the change in the degree of trust value, the trust value will be dynamically increased or decreased. 

