\subsection{Mel-to-Audio Consistency Verification}

To verify the alignment between mel-spectrogram frame count and audio frame count, we tracked the following:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $\text{mel\_length} = \text{waveform\_length} / \text{hop\_size}$
    \item All inference samples conformed to this relationship.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Conclusion}

After validating inference logs, comparing mel frame counts, and matching waveform durations, we ruled out issues in pre-processing, STFT padding, or inference time truncation. These observations suggest that the previously reported duration anomaly is not caused by implementation bugs, but likely arises from training data mismatch, activational bias (e.g., LeakyReLU vs. Snake), or temporal extrapolation failure specific to HiFi-GAN under long-term generation settings.


